Kevin Wayne wrote:
> What potions do you think are worth diluting, and which ones are worth
> saving?
> 
> I tend to dilute:
> 
> Booze (saving a couple for self-confusion in the early game)
> Fruit juice
> See invisible (usually get that as an intrinsic in the Mines)
> Sickness

These ones depend on what alignment I'm playing. An orcish Rogue can 
find some nice application for these potions.

> Confusion
> Hallucination
> Restore Ability (use unihorns for that)
> Sleeping
> Blindness
> Invisibility (zap self with wand when I have the chance)
> Monster Detection
> Object Detection (rethinking this)

I keep a few of these in case I get something stolen or can't find 
something I was sure I was having. Also can server as some indication of 
monster detection...

> Levitation

These depend... If I don't have any other source of levitation, I either 
fall down trapdoors on Medusa's level, or keep these potions. (That's a 
Murphy's xor, btw.).

> Acid
> Oil (unless I don't have a permanent light source)
> Paralysis
> 
